00:00:39.731 --> 00:00:42.993
- [Voiceover] Erik asks, "Do you 
believe in Jim Collins' belief

00:00:42.993 --> 00:00:45.279
that you can only focus on three things?"

00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:50.394
Erik, as a very underread,
undereducated gentleman,

00:00:50.394 --> 00:00:52.536
I don't know all the details

00:00:52.536 --> 00:00:55.439
of Mr. Collins' three
things that we can focus

00:00:55.439 --> 00:00:56.738
or the thesis behind it

00:00:56.738 --> 00:00:58.816
but I will tell you that

00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:01.259
I'm a contradiction on this question.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.465
Oftentimes I think that

00:01:03.465 --> 00:01:04.882
if you're doing more than one thing,

00:01:04.882 --> 00:01:06.542
you're not doing anything,

00:01:06.542 --> 00:01:08.944
and so when I focus on
building businesses,

00:01:08.944 --> 00:01:11.962
I try to focus on one core
thing, but look at me right now,

00:01:11.962 --> 00:01:13.518
I've never been busier in my life

00:01:13.518 --> 00:01:16.906
and I've decided to
start another video show?

00:01:16.906 --> 00:01:19.578
Here's my theory: focus on one thing,

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:22.023
and make that 80-90% of your nut,

00:01:22.023 --> 00:01:27.023
and then have 20%, 10-20%
of complete and utter chaos

00:01:27.608 --> 00:01:29.348
trying things, probably losing

00:01:29.348 --> 00:01:30.927
because you're not focused on them,

00:01:30.927 --> 00:01:33.555
but it keeps life spicy and interesting.

00:01:33.555 --> 00:01:35.299
That's what works for me.

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:36.782
The truth is, I have a feeling this works

00:01:36.782 --> 00:01:39.001
very differently for everyone.

00:01:39.001 --> 00:01:41.100
- [Voiceover] Corey asks, 
"What's the best way

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.729
to grow a following or a
community from nothing?"

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:46.326
Corey, this is easy for me to answer,

00:01:46.326 --> 00:01:48.403
since I've done it a couple of times,

00:01:48.403 --> 00:01:52.872
and the real answer is,
content and context.

00:01:52.872 --> 00:01:54.893
My belief is the best way to
build a following right now

00:01:54.893 --> 00:01:57.675
is to put out daily, if you can, content

00:01:57.675 --> 00:02:00.136
and get as close to
that as possible, right,

00:02:00.136 --> 00:02:02.887
and so, every day, put out your picture

00:02:02.887 --> 00:02:06.033
or your drawing on your
Snapchat that you blast out

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:09.168
or your Instagram photos
or your video show

00:02:09.168 --> 00:02:12.573
or whatever you may be
doing. Your written blog,

00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:14.598
every day. You know?

00:02:14.598 --> 00:02:16.339
Six days is better than five days,

00:02:16.339 --> 00:02:17.733
and five days is better than four days,

00:02:17.733 --> 00:02:19.195
and four days is better than three days,

00:02:19.195 --> 00:02:22.353
and two days is better
than one day a week.

00:02:22.353 --> 00:02:24.373
But if you're doing it one
or two or three days a week,

00:02:24.373 --> 00:02:25.614
are you really doing it?

00:02:25.614 --> 00:02:27.612
And so pumping out hardcore content,

00:02:27.612 --> 00:02:29.620
and then engaging.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.733
I'm going to ask a
Question of the Day today,

00:02:31.733 --> 00:02:34.960
and hopefully, after I get
home at 11:30, twelve tonight,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.435
I'm gonna go into the comments

00:02:36.435 --> 00:02:38.419
and reply to some of those answers,

00:02:38.419 --> 00:02:39.998
creating context.

00:02:39.998 --> 00:02:43.179
You've empowered me by watching my show,

00:02:43.179 --> 00:02:45.211
I then jumped back in to answer

00:02:45.211 --> 00:02:47.335
your Question of the Day answer,

00:02:47.335 --> 00:02:49.855
showing you that I appreciate you.

00:02:49.855 --> 00:02:51.619
We've created a deeper context,

00:02:51.619 --> 00:02:54.196
just like when I reply to
you or I answer your email

00:02:54.196 --> 00:02:56.912
or some of the Cyber Dusts
I've done in the last 24 hours,

00:02:56.912 --> 00:02:59.338
it's about content and context.

00:02:59.338 --> 00:03:01.371
Building a community takes work.

00:03:01.371 --> 00:03:04.712
Building a community is
not a foregone conclusion.

00:03:04.712 --> 00:03:06.314
Everybody just thinks
you're gonna start a show

00:03:06.314 --> 00:03:07.591
and everything's gonna magically happen,

00:03:07.591 --> 00:03:08.963
or you're gonna start a blog

00:03:08.963 --> 00:03:11.261
or you're gonna become
an Instagram sensation.

00:03:11.261 --> 00:03:12.702
The talent to put out the content

00:03:12.702 --> 00:03:14.883
is only one piece of the equation.

00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:19.893
1% of the magic 1%, get it
just by the content push-out,

00:03:19.898 --> 00:03:22.904
but for the rest of us
chaps and chapettes,

00:03:22.904 --> 00:03:24.600
we've gotta put in the
work into the community

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.118
and care back to the
time they've allocated.

00:03:27.118 --> 00:03:30.161
The fact that people are spending
ten minutes to watch this

00:03:30.161 --> 00:03:32.865
in your ridiculously busy world

00:03:32.865 --> 00:03:36.337
is something I will never,
ever take for granted.

