and I'm not trying to sting,

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.573
but it might feel a little like that.

00:05:32.066 --> 00:05:33.329
(laughs)

00:05:33.329 --> 00:05:37.383
Trying to make a right
hook feel like a jab

00:05:37.383 --> 00:05:42.130
is what 99% of salespeople
and businesses do

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.463
that end up failing.

00:05:44.463 --> 00:05:49.284
It is in the clear honesty
and clear track of,

00:05:49.284 --> 00:05:53.545
"when I want to do something
nice for you, I just do it,"

00:05:53.545 --> 00:05:55.449
Ă&nbsp; la this show.

00:05:55.449 --> 00:05:57.969
I just wanna take 15-20 minutes of my day

00:05:57.969 --> 00:06:01.253
to share the God-given wisdom
and the work experience

00:06:01.253 --> 00:06:05.828
and I want all of you to watch
it and I want this in return.

00:06:05.828 --> 00:06:09.750
Now, come 15 months from
now, 18 months from now,

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.486
whether it's a book,
whether it's a seminar,

00:06:12.486 --> 00:06:15.851
whether it's an event, whether
it's me selling rare toys,

00:06:15.851 --> 00:06:17.988
who knows what it might be,

00:06:17.988 --> 00:06:19.485
then I will clearly say,

00:06:19.485 --> 00:06:24.105
"buy this friggin' rare toy,
it's $9.99. Buy it now."

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:28.564
But up until that point,
I will have very clear -

00:06:28.719 --> 00:06:31.297
there'll be no show where
you're watching the show

00:06:31.297 --> 00:06:34.280
and behind the scenes right
now there's subliminal music

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.219
pumping, "buy the damn cat for $9.99".

00:06:37.219 --> 00:06:38.437
There is none of that.

00:06:38.437 --> 00:06:41.445
And so there's a massive confusion
in the marketplace, Bill,

00:06:41.445 --> 00:06:43.558
that people want to disguise the sale,

00:06:43.558 --> 00:06:45.124
and there is no disguise.

00:06:45.124 --> 00:06:48.606
Authentically. All in. All of it.

00:06:48.606 --> 00:06:51.973
All in. Give when it's time to give.

00:06:51.973 --> 00:06:55.177
On the flip side, there is
a crapload of Mother Teresas

00:06:55.177 --> 00:06:57.580
and think it's so nice and awesome

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.461
and if you're just good, it's gonna - no.

00:06:59.461 --> 00:07:00.685
You need to sell.

00:07:00.685 --> 00:07:03.007
So when you sell, you say, I'm selling.

00:07:03.007 --> 00:07:05.619
I am selling this. And I feel comfortable.

00:07:05.619 --> 00:07:08.543
When I put a link out,
buy my book. It's out.

00:07:08.543 --> 00:07:11.319
Buy it. If I've done
anything for you, buy it.

00:07:11.319 --> 00:07:14.627
So, the answer to your
question is very simple.

00:07:14.627 --> 00:07:16.125
There is no version of that.

00:07:16.125 --> 00:07:18.422
That is a losing mentality and execution

00:07:18.422 --> 00:07:20.525
and I highly recommend that you take it

00:07:20.525 --> 00:07:23.079
and you split it very hard apart

00:07:23.079 --> 00:07:24.448
where the jabs are clear

00:07:24.448 --> 00:07:26.898
and where the right hooks are clear.

00:07:26.898 --> 00:07:30.705
- [Voiceover] Jason asks, "how can a 
public or government institution

00:07:30.705 --> 00:07:33.597
use social media more effectively
in marketing campaigns,

00:07:33.597 --> 00:07:36.006
i.e. to increase voter turnout?"

00:07:36.998 --> 00:07:41.781
- Jason, the truth to that
answer is, believe it or not,

00:07:41.781 --> 00:07:44.254
is to become more nimble and authentic.

00:07:44.254 --> 00:07:46.494
There is no campaign

00:07:46.494 --> 00:07:49.640
when there isn't the right process up top.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:53.400
What I mean by that is, a lot
of government institutions

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.712
are coming from the wrong place.

00:07:55.712 --> 00:07:57.233
For example,

00:07:57.233 --> 00:08:00.100
I know that, you know, just
from a little politics,

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:02.455
and I don't talk politics very often,

00:08:02.455 --> 00:08:04.614
but, like, that the Democratic Party

00:08:04.614 --> 00:08:06.948
wants more voter turnout

00:08:06.948 --> 00:08:09.153
and the Republican Party
historically has not.

00:08:09.153 --> 00:08:11.708
These are little tidbits I've
picked up in the last 12 years

00:08:11.708 --> 00:08:12.833
and I could be wrong about that,

00:08:12.833 --> 00:08:14.611
they're just people in the game

00:08:14.611 --> 00:08:16.395
that I've heard things like that.

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:20.325
So where are you coming
from is really the question.

00:08:20.325 --> 00:08:24.631
I mean, to use social
to attract more voters,

00:08:24.631 --> 00:08:26.732
the truth is, whether you're
a Republican or a Democrat,

00:08:26.732 --> 00:08:29.148
you're trying to not recruit more voters,

00:08:29.148 --> 00:08:30.703
you're trying to recruit more voters

00:08:30.703 --> 00:08:32.467
that are gonna vote for you.

00:08:32.467 --> 00:08:33.547
Right?

00:08:33.547 --> 00:08:36.868
And so right there by its own definition,

00:08:36.868 --> 00:08:40.582
you've got an interesting
kind of perplex situation

00:08:40.582 --> 00:08:43.751
that the seed is tainted by the outcome.

00:08:43.751 --> 00:08:46.423
And so to the best of one's ability,

00:08:46.423 --> 00:08:50.821
I think it's important to try
to get the religion at the top

00:08:50.821 --> 00:08:52.122
to really execute.

00:08:52.122 --> 00:08:53.306
I mean, look,

00:08:53.306 --> 00:08:57.044
social media is probably the
most consumer-insight-driven

00:08:57.044 --> 00:08:58.807
marketing tool we've ever seen.

00:08:58.807 --> 00:09:01.002
The data that you can
apply on top of social

00:09:01.002 --> 00:09:02.070
to drive the results,

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.287
whether to get somebody
to vote for an election,

00:09:04.287 --> 00:09:07.805
to buy a cat, to whatever it may be,

00:09:07.805 --> 00:09:09.280
there's never been anything greater,

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:14.007
and so using, I've said it
before, Facebook dark posts,

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:19.831
with a combination of
Google long-tail search SEM,

00:09:19.831 --> 00:09:22.579
can get you very, very, very far.

